{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_replicated_event_sourcing_conflict_resolver_conflictresolver", "label": "ConflictResolver", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/replicated-event-sourcing/conflict-resolver.mdx", "source_location": "## The interface", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The strategy that reconciles a concurrent pair into one event - a winner or a synthesised merge. Single type parameter (the event, not the state); when more than two events are concurrent the framework folds them pairwise so the whole set reduces to one winning event, applied through the normal onEvent. Runs only on concurrent-write detection, so it is cheap next to journal I/O."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_replicated_event_sourcing_conflict_resolver_conflictcandidate", "label": "ConflictCandidate", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/replicated-event-sourcing/conflict-resolver.mdx", "source_location": "## The interface", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Carries event, timestamp (wall-clock at the originating replica), replica id and the vector clock at persist time - the data a resolver must decide from."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_replicated_event_sourcing_conflict_resolver_deterministiccommutativecontract", "label": "Deterministic + commutative resolver contract", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/replicated-event-sourcing/conflict-resolver.mdx", "source_location": "## Two hard contracts", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "resolve must be deterministic (no Date.now, no Math.random, no external reads) so every replica agrees, and commutative because events arrive in different orders on different replicas - a non-commutative resolver makes replicas diverge. Decide from the candidates' own data, never from arrival order or 'prefer a'."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_replicated_event_sourcing_conflict_resolver_lastwriterwinsresolver", "label": "LastWriterWinsResolver (default)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/replicated-event-sourcing/conflict-resolver.mdx", "source_location": "### `LastWriterWinsResolver` (default)", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Higher timestamp wins; on a tie the higher lexicographic replica id, so every replica converges. Relies on roughly comparable wall clocks across replicas - the same trade-off as LWWRegister."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_replicated_event_sourcing_conflict_resolver_custommergeresolver", "label": "CustomMergeResolver", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/replicated-event-sourcing/conflict-resolver.mdx", "source_location": "### `CustomMergeResolver`", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Wraps a commutative merge of the two payloads for domain knowledge LWW cannot capture. It sorts the candidates by replica id before calling the merge, so the function sees a deterministic argument order even when it is not perfectly symmetric - the contract still says be commutative."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_replicated_event_sourcing_conflict_resolver_highestwins", "label": "HighestWins custom resolver", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/replicated-event-sourcing/conflict-resolver.mdx", "source_location": "### Pick a winner (max / min)", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "For values that must not regress - stock levels, high scores - with an exact tie broken on replica id so the result is the same everywhere."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_replicated_event_sourcing_conflict_resolver_orderedwins", "label": "OrderedWins custom resolver", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/replicated-event-sourcing/conflict-resolver.mdx", "source_location": "### Deterministic order by (timestamp, replica)", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Deterministic order by (timestamp, replica) - shown as the template for your own tie-breaking."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_replicated_event_sourcing_conflict_resolver_mergewrongabstraction", "label": "When a merge is the wrong abstraction", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/replicated-event-sourcing/conflict-resolver.mdx", "source_location": "## When a merge is the wrong abstraction", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Some concurrent events conflict semantically ('close account' concurrent with 'deposit') and should not merge at all. Use replicated ES when concurrent events merge naturally; use the single-writer lease when they should not happen."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_replicated_event_sourcing_conflict_resolver_conflictresolver", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_replicated_event_sourcing_conflict_resolver_conflictcandidate", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/replicated-event-sourcing/conflict-resolver.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_replicated_event_sourcing_conflict_resolver_conflictresolver", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_replicated_event_sourcing_conflict_resolver_deterministiccommutativecontract", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/replicated-event-sourcing/conflict-resolver.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_replicated_event_sourcing_conflict_resolver_lastwriterwinsresolver", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_replicated_event_sourcing_conflict_resolver_conflictresolver", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/replicated-event-sourcing/conflict-resolver.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_replicated_event_sourcing_conflict_resolver_custommergeresolver", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_replicated_event_sourcing_conflict_resolver_conflictresolver", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/replicated-event-sourcing/conflict-resolver.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_replicated_event_sourcing_conflict_resolver_highestwins", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_replicated_event_sourcing_conflict_resolver_conflictresolver", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/replicated-event-sourcing/conflict-resolver.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_replicated_event_sourcing_conflict_resolver_orderedwins", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_replicated_event_sourcing_conflict_resolver_conflictresolver", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/replicated-event-sourcing/conflict-resolver.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_replicated_event_sourcing_conflict_resolver_orderedwins", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_replicated_event_sourcing_conflict_resolver_lastwriterwinsresolver", "relation": "semantically_similar_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/replicated-event-sourcing/conflict-resolver.mdx", "source_location": "### Deterministic order by (timestamp, replica)", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_replicated_event_sourcing_conflict_resolver_conflictresolver", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_replicated_event_sourcing_conflict_resolver_mergewrongabstraction", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/replicated-event-sourcing/conflict-resolver.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_replicated_event_sourcing_conflict_resolver_mergewrongabstraction", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_replicated_event_sourcing_single_writer_lease_singlewriterlease", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/replicated-event-sourcing/conflict-resolver.mdx", "source_location": "## When a merge is the wrong abstraction", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_replicated_event_sourcing_conflict_resolver_conflictresolver", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_replicated_event_sourcing_vector_clocks_vectorclock", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/replicated-event-sourcing/conflict-resolver.mdx", "source_location": "intro", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_replicated_event_sourcing_conflict_resolver_conflictresolver", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_persistent_actor_onevent", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/replicated-event-sourcing/conflict-resolver.mdx", "source_location": "## The interface", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_replicated_event_sourcing_conflict_resolver_conflictresolver", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_replicated_event_sourcing_snapshotting_replicatedsnapshot", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/replicated-event-sourcing/conflict-resolver.mdx", "source_location": "## Where to next", "weight": 1.0}], "hyperedges": []}